      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "East Asians, particularly those from China, Japan, and Korea, tend to exhibit a more collectivist and stoic temperament in high-pressure professional settings, often prioritizing group harmony and avoiding conflict over individual success. This is rooted in their cultural values emphasizing social hierarchy, respect for authority, and self-control. In contrast, individuals from Mediterranean backgrounds, such as Greeks and Italians, are often characterized by a more expressive and assertive personality, valuing social relationships and emotional expression in the workplace. This difference in temperament can lead to varying coping mechanisms and stress responses in high-stress environments.",
